      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/util/auditLog.ts exports: (a) getAuditLogPath(): string returning $XDG_STATE_HOME/verse8/mcp.log with ~/.local/state/verse8/mcp.log fallback; (b) projectDirDigest(projectDir: string): string returning sha256(projectDir).slice(0,12); (c) appendAuditLine(entry: AuditEntry): void that writes one JSON line and rotates when size >= 1MB.",
        "File is opened with mode 0o600; directories are created with mode 0o700.",
        "Rotation: when pre-write size >= 1MB, rename current to mcp.log.1 (replacing any existing .1), then start fresh mcp.log. Only one rotated file retained.",
        "All I/O errors are swallowed (non-fatal) — writer returns without throwing. Audit failure must never block tool path.",
        "projectDirDigest('/tmp/foo/bar') returns a deterministic 12-char hex prefix of sha256('/tmp/foo/bar').",
        "Audit entries contain at minimum: ts (ISO), tool, outcome ('ok'|'error'), durationMs (number), projectDirDigest (string|undefined), correlationId (string), error (ErrorCode|undefined). Never raw projectDir. Never tokens (writer routes `hint`-like fields through util/redact safeHint).",
        "tests/unit/auditLog.test.mjs has ≥6 cases covering: digest determinism, write+read one line, rotation at 1MB threshold (drops old .1), non-fatal when directory is read-only, environment override VERSE8_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, appendAuditLine redacts token-shaped values in entry.hint.",
        "VERSE8_AUDIT_LOG_PATH env override supported (test uses it to isolate each case in a tmpdir).",
        "tsc compiles cleanly.",
        "AC-OBSERVABILITY-2 + AC-OBSERVABILITY-3 met (rotation + digest)."
      ]
